  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1028 PM MDT Wed Oct 21 2026\n\nA very active weather pattern will bring a widespread chance of \nstrong thunderstorms and heavy rain to Southern New Mexico and Far\nWest Texas Thursday through Saturday. A deep moist southerly flow\ncontinues between a strong ridge of high pressure over central \nTexas and a deep low pressure system centered along the California\ncoast. As the low pressure system begins to move inland. \nScattered to numerous showers will occur over Arizona and western \nportions of New Mexico northward into the Great Basin and parts of\nColorado. Favorable forcing and lift will interact with the moist\nunstable air mass to generate widespread thunderstorms across the\nlocal area in the afternoon and evening. The highest amount of \nactivity will be concentrated in the Gila region and nearby areas \nmostly west of Rio Grande extending to the Arizona Border. \n\nThere is a a marginal risk of severe thunderstorms for areas west\nof the Rio Grande on Thursday with possible large hail, strong\nwind gusts, and maybe a low probability short lived weak tornado.\nWidespread thunderstorms will also produce periods of heavy rain\nwith a potential for flash flooding, especially in the Gila Region\nand nearby surrounding areas. A flash flood watch is in effect for\nthat area from noon Thursday through 6am Friday morning. Potential\nrain amounts are between 1 and 2 inches with isolated higher \namounts in the Gila Region.   \n\nThe active weather pattern will continue on Friday widespread\nshowers and thunderstorms over portions of south central  New \nMexico centered on the Rio Grande valley from El Paso north to \nAlbuquerque. There will be a marginal risk of severe thunderstorms\nFriday afternoon and evening. There will also be a chance of \nexcessive rainfall with a potential for flooding. \n\nA similar situation will develop on Saturday with additional\nexcessive rainfall with a potential for flooding for areas\ngenerally east of the Rio Grande. Strong thunderstorms with large\nhail and strong winds will be also be possible. \n\nThe low pressure system and the moisture will lift out of the\nlocal area Sunday in to Monday with a return drier and calmer\nweather conditions for a few days. Long term outlook does have a\nchance of showers returning late next week.",
